1. Create a basic webpage

Add the HTML document structure, a page title, one main heading, and two paragraphs.

2. Style headings and paragraphs

Make the heading blue, center it, and set paragraph text to 18px.

3. Create a personal profile

Add your name, a short bio, and a profile image with suitable alt text.

4. Create a navigation menu

Add three links: Home, About, and Contact. Place each link on the same line.

5. Build a student card

Use a div containing a name, course, and button. Add a background color, padding, border, and rounded corners.

6. Practice the CSS box model

Create a box with width 300px, padding 20px, a 3px solid border, and margin 30px.

7. Create a list

Show at least five favorite hobbies using an unordered list. Change its text color using CSS.

8. Build a contact form

Add fields for name, email, and password, plus a submit button. Use labels for the fields.

9. Practice IDs in CSS

Give a heading the ID page-title and a paragraph the ID intro. Style them separately using # selectors.